WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.199 --> 00:00:12.199
In this part of our tutorial we're going to talk about object oriented concepts as this is important to understand but not get a masterful meaning of

2
00:00:12.199 --> 00:00:23.199
mainly in the terms of vocabulary and what I mean by that is something called a parent slash child class relationship.

3
00:00:23.199 --> 00:00:30.199
Now in the diagram over here we have a biological family and this family has traits.

4
00:00:30.199 --> 00:00:38.259
So the parents are the rectangular things up at the top and they have the ability to be blue, red or green.

5
00:00:38.259 --> 00:00:47.359
Now underneath them are their children. So their children you can see here they have the ability to be red, blue or green

6
00:00:47.359 --> 00:00:55.359
but there isn't the ability for them to select purple or orange or pink or some other color

7
00:00:55.359 --> 00:01:00.359
because that is not a trait that was passed down to the children so they don't have that to choose from.

8
00:01:00.359 --> 00:01:07.519
Now again this is a very simplistic look at how biology passes traits from their parents down to children

9
00:01:07.519 --> 00:01:11.519
but the same thing can be applied to our code.

10
00:01:11.519 --> 00:01:19.519
Inside of Unreal any class can be derived from making it a parent class and we can do this with blueprints

11
00:01:19.519 --> 00:01:29.319
and the reason that we want to do this is a parent class can do things like set default values or predefined data or functions

12
00:01:29.319 --> 00:01:37.319
that we want to start off with and then approve upon or adjust or even completely modify inside of the child.

13
00:01:37.319 --> 00:01:46.319
This is because again a child is derived from an existing class and inside of a child we can override the parent's functionality

14
00:01:46.319 --> 00:01:56.319
or default properties and this allows a child to extend the parent class or get more functionality out of it.

15
00:01:56.319 --> 00:02:02.739
All classes are the child of another actor inside of Unreal up until UObject.

16
00:02:02.739 --> 00:02:11.740
So UObject is the one master object so to speak or the master parent and everything is a child of UObject.

17
00:02:11.740 --> 00:02:21.250
Now inheritance is something I further want to touch on as this is something that you're going to definitely come in contact

18
00:02:21.250 --> 00:02:26.250
and you're already most likely using inside of all of your Unreal Engine projects

19
00:02:26.250 --> 00:02:35.659
and inheritance is simply receiving variables, functions or macros, components and even default settings

20
00:02:35.659 --> 00:02:48.069
from the class that is above it or its parent class and then utilizing those to do something interesting inside of the child.

21
00:02:48.069 --> 00:02:56.300
One of the other things to keep in mind is that any changes to the parent will affect the child

22
00:02:56.300 --> 00:03:05.300
unless the child overrides that value. So if we have a parent value set for health to 100,

23
00:03:05.300 --> 00:03:12.300
child's default value for health is always going to be 100 unless they override that value.

24
00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:19.330
If we decide at some point to change that health value to 120, all of the children that are made from that parent

25
00:03:19.330 --> 00:03:24.330
will have that updated unless we've decided to change that health value to say something like 80.

26
00:03:24.330 --> 00:03:32.330
All of the ones that we have changed will have that health value of 80 while all the rest will still have that new health value of 120.
